MongoDB-Specific Security

* Never pass unvalidated user-supplied objects directly into MongoDB queries.
* Never accept arbitrary query operators from clients.
* Use explicit query filters and allowlisted fields.
* Prevent unauthorized mass assignment.
* Validate ObjectIds and record ownership.
* Avoid exposing internal database errors.
* Apply least-privilege database credentials.
* Keep MongoDB Atlas access appropriately restricted.
* Never disable database authentication or network restrictions for convenience.

Vercel-Specific Security

* Keep secrets in Vercel server-side environment variables.
* Never expose secret variables through NEXT_PUBLIC_.
* Do not store sessions, payments, or permanent files only in process memory or local filesystem.
* Ensure privileged routes execute server-side.
* Do not rely on middleware alone for final authorization.
* Recheck permissions in every sensitive API and service operation.
* Use a durable shared rate-limiting mechanism where required; do not rely solely on in-memory counters across serverless instances.

